{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Et YHWH your Elohim you shall fear.</b> Not to transgress a negative commandment." "<b>Him you shall serve.</b> Through a positive commandment." "<b>And in Him you shall cleave.</b> In the heart. Another interpretation: since it wrote just above some of the ways of HaKadosh Barukh Hu, therefore it writes here <b>and in Him you shall cleave</b> — that is, you shall cleave to His ways and act like Him. But in the section of Va'etchanan it did not write of His ways at all; therefore it wrote there only 'Him you shall serve and in His name you shall swear.'" "<b>And in His name you shall swear.</b> With the mouth. And if you ask: is it not written 'לא תשא את שם' etc.? Rather, when the inclination overpowers you to transgress a sin, then you are permitted to swear in His name so that you not commit the transgression, as Boaz did."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:22.982184012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}